---
import Read from '../layouts/Read.astro';
import PlainForm from '../components/PlainForm.astro';
import { cards, thinkers, questions } from '../lib/atlas.js';
import { lessonsByModule } from '../lib/lessons.js';
const lessons = Object.values(lessonsByModule).reduce((n, l) => n + l.length, 0);
---
<Read title="Support Svapna — free to read, kept open by its readers" description="Svapna is free and donation-supported, in the spirit of dāna. A coffee covers hosting; sharing it or writing for the library helps as much." path="/support" crumbs={[{ name: 'Support', path: '/support' }]}>
  <p class="small crumb"><a href="/">Svapna</a> · Support</p>
  <h1>Given freely, <em>passed forward.</em></h1>
  <p class="lede">Dāna is the Sanskrit for generosity: not a transaction, a circulation. Everything here is open to anyone. If it has served you, the way to thank it is to keep it open for the next person.</p>
  <p><a class="go big" href="https://www.buymeacoffee.com/svapna" target="_blank" rel="noopener" data-pirsch-event="coffee_click">Buy a coffee ↗</a></p>

  <section>
    <h2>Other ways</h2>
    <div class="steps">
      <div><b>Share it</b><div><p>Send Svapna to one person who would use it.</p><button class="go" id="share" type="button">Share the link →</button></div></div>
      <div><b>Write for the library</b><div><p>Pitch an essay on a tradition, a text or a finding the library is missing.</p><PlainForm id="pitch" subject="[Library] Pitch" button="Send the pitch" messageLabel="The idea, in a few lines" done="Thank you. The pitch has arrived." /></div></div>
      <div><b>Correct it</b><div><p>A wrong quote, date, place or reading is worth more than a coffee.</p><a class="go" href="/about/contact">Send a correction →</a></div></div>
    </div>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>What it keeps open</h2>
    <p class="def">{cards.length} passages from {thinkers.length} thinkers and texts, each checked against its source; {questions.length} questions; {lessons} lessons on the history of dreaming; a glossary and a library. All of it free to read, with no advertising and nothing sold. <a href="/how-it-works">How it is made</a>.</p>
  </section>

  <section>
    <h2>Where it goes</h2>
    <p class="def">Svapna is made by Flint, an independent researcher working alone. What it costs to keep open: the AI research tools that find passages and check every quote against its source, which are the largest part; the domain; and hosting and email. Contributions go to those. It is not a registered nonprofit, and contributions are not tax-deductible. <a href="/about/acknowledgments">Acknowledgments</a> · <a href="/how-it-works">How it is made</a>.</p>
  </section>
  <script is:inline>
    (function () { var b = document.getElementById('share'), u = 'https://svapnaproject.org', t = 'Svapna — the big questions, and the history of dreaming';
      function flash(m) { var o = b.textContent; b.textContent = m; setTimeout(function () { b.textContent = o; }, 2000); }
      b.addEventListener('click', function () {
        if (navigator.share) { navigator.share({ url: u, title: t }).catch(function () {}); return; }
        navigator.clipboard.writeText(u).then(function () { flash('Link copied'); }, function () { flash('Copy failed'); });
      }); })();
  </script>
</Read>
